"""Part 3, group 7: the automatic tests."""
GROUP = "7 · Tests and automatic checks"

TEST_BASICS = (
    "How Django tests work: each `class ...Tests(TestCase)` groups tests; each method whose name starts "
    "with `test_` is one test. `python manage.py test` finds and runs them all, each in a temporary database "
    "that is emptied afterwards, so tests never touch your real data. A test does something, then checks "
    "the result with `self.assertEqual(actual, expected)` and similar; if a check fails, the test fails and "
    "says why. `SimpleTestCase` is for tests that don't need a database. `setUpTestData` prepares data once "
    "for all of a class's tests; `setUp` runs before each test. `@override_settings(...)` changes settings "
    "for one class or test. `mock.patch(...)` swaps a real function for a stand-in while a test runs."
)

